Scenario: escapeHTMLTest1 | Verifies that special HTML characters are escaped.
GIVEN a string containing HTML tags, double quotes, an ampersand, and single quotes.
WHEN escapeHTML is called with the string.
THEN the characters are replaced with their corresponding HTML entities.

Scenario: escapeHTMLTest2 | Verifies that null input is handled by escapeHTML.
GIVEN a null string.
WHEN escapeHTML is called.
THEN an empty string is returned.

Scenario: createPageTest1 | Verifies that a complete HTML page is generated.
GIVEN a page title and HTML body content.
WHEN createPage is called.
THEN a complete HTML document is returned with the specified title, metadata, and body content.

Scenario: createPageTest2 | Verifies that the page title is escaped and null body content is handled.
GIVEN a title containing angle brackets and a null body.
WHEN createPage is called.
THEN the title is HTML-escaped and the body contains a whitespace character.

Scenario: createHeadingTest1 | Verifies that a heading is generated from plain text.
GIVEN the text "Hello World".
WHEN createHeading is called.
THEN an h1 element containing "Hello World" is returned.

Scenario: createHeadingTest2 | Verifies that heading text is HTML-escaped.
GIVEN the text "<script>".
WHEN createHeading is called.
THEN an h1 element containing "&lt;script&gt;" is returned.

Scenario: createTextBlockTest1 | Verifies that multiline text is wrapped in a pre element.
GIVEN the text "Line 1" followed by "Line 2" on a new line.
WHEN createTextBlock is called.
THEN the text is returned inside a pre element with the newline preserved.

Scenario: createTextBlockTest2 | Verifies that text containing HTML tags is escaped.
GIVEN the text "<script>".
WHEN createTextBlock is called.
THEN the script tag is escaped inside a pre element.

Scenario: createLinkTest1 | Verifies that a link is generated from a URL and label.
GIVEN the URL "/browse" and label "Browse Records".
WHEN createLink is called.
THEN an anchor element with the specified URL and label is returned.

Scenario: createLinkTest2 | Verifies that special characters in a link URL and label are escaped.
GIVEN a URL containing an ampersand and a label containing angle brackets.
WHEN createLink is called.
THEN the ampersand in the URL and the angle brackets in the label are HTML-escaped.

Scenario: createLinkListTest1 | Verifies that a list of links is generated.
GIVEN links to the agents and missions pages with their labels.
WHEN createLinkList is called.
THEN an unordered list containing both links is returned.

Scenario: createLinkListTest2 | Verifies that null input produces an empty link list.
GIVEN a null array of links.
WHEN createLinkList is called.
THEN an empty unordered list is returned.

Scenario: createLinkListTest3 | Verifies that invalid link entries are skipped.
GIVEN an array containing a valid link, a null entry, an entry with only a URL, and another valid link.
WHEN createLinkList is called.
THEN the null entry and incomplete entry are skipped, and the two valid links are returned in an unordered list.

Scenario: createIDFormTest1 | Verifies that an ID input form is generated.
GIVEN the action "/read" and label "Enter ID:".
WHEN createIDForm is called.
THEN a GET form is returned with the specified action, a required numeric ID input, and a Read button.

Scenario: createIDFormTest2 | Verifies that special characters in an ID form's action and label are escaped.
GIVEN an action containing an ampersand and a label containing angle brackets.
WHEN createIDForm is called.
THEN the action and label are HTML-escaped in the generated GET form.

Scenario: createReadFormTest1 | Verifies that a record-reading form is generated for a specified type.
GIVEN the record type "Agent".
WHEN createReadForm is called.
THEN a GET form is returned with a hidden type field, an Agent ID label, a required numeric ID input, and a Read button.

Scenario: createBackLinkTest1 | Verifies that a link to the main menu is generated.
GIVEN no additional input.
WHEN createBackLink is called.
THEN a link to "/" with the label "Back to Main Menu" is returned.